      "path": "src/ui/screens/TradeDetail.tsx",
      "content": "A terminal disposition means the position is closed, not that its contract has expired. An option sold or bought back before expiration will also take this branch and display, for example, “Expired Fri 20 Nov 2026” while that date is still in the future. Choose the expiration wording from the expiration/settlement state rather than the presence of terminalDisposition, and cover a FullyDisposedPreExpiration trade.",
      "existing_code": "      {contract \u0026\u0026 !settlementPanel \u0026\u0026 \u003cp\u003e{`${'terminalDisposition' in view ? 'Expired' : 'Expires'} ${expirationDate(contract.expiration)}`}\u003c/p\u003e}",
      "start_line": 316,
      "end_line": 316,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/TradeDetail.tsx",
      "content": "The incoherent-detail branch still renders only executions, so recorded expirations disappear from the fact history when replay fails. recordedPositionChanges retains settlement-bearing changes, and IncoherentPanel only lists findings; neither exposes these settlement rows. Render SettlementSection with view.recordedPositionChanges here as well, so users can inspect the authoritative expiration facts even for an incoherent trade.",
      "existing_code": "          \u003cExecutionsSection positionChanges={view.recordedPositionChanges} journal={outcomesOnly(view.journal)} legs={view.plan.legs} timeZone={timeZone} /\u003e",
      "start_line": 215,
      "end_line": 215,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/option-disposition.ts",
      "content": "This introduces a nested ternary, which the review checklist explicitly prohibits. Handle `Expiration` with an early return, then select `sale` or `buyback` in a separate expression to keep the mechanism mapping straightforward.",
      "suggestion_code": "const mechanismWord = (side: 'Long' | 'Short', mechanism: Mechanisms[number]['mechanism']): string =\u003e {\n  if (mechanism === 'Expiration') return 'expiration';\n  return side === 'Long' ? 'sale' : 'buyback';\n};",
